BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 500.0 Td (pads, effort-based grip detection and a coordinated impedance controller.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 0.100 0.200 0.350 rg 46.0 485.4 Td (Motion planning) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 485.4 Td (Analytic inverse kinematics with hand-designed choreography; no MoveIt 2, therefore no general collision-aware planning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 472.8 Td (Base-deck and arm-crossing collisions are avoided by staging poses and staggered deployment rather than by a planner.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 0.100 0.200 0.350 rg 46.0 458.2 Td (Navigation) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 458.2 Td (Odometry plus LiDAR docking; no SLAM, no global map, no Nav2 obstacle avoidance. Adequate for an open floor, not for a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 445.6 Td (cluttered room.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 0.100 0.200 0.350 rg 46.0 431.0 Td (Object pose assumption) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 431.0 Td (Objects are assumed to lie with their long axis pointing toward the approach direction, which the central scan hub enforces.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 418.4 Td (Arbitrary in-plane orientation would need point-cloud pose estimation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 0.100 0.200 0.350 rg 46.0 403.8 Td (Perception modality) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 403.8 Td (Single-colour segmentation per object class; sensitive to lighting and to palette collisions with the environment, as encountered) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 391.2 Td (during development.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 0.100 0.200 0.350 rg 46.0 376.6 Td (Orientation authority) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 376.6 Td (4-DOF per arm \(yaw plus three coplanar pitches\) provides planar orientation only - sufficient for the sideways-to-upright task, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 364.0 Td (for general 3D reorientation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 0.100 0.200 0.350 rg 46.0 349.4 Td (Self-collision) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 349.4 Td (Disabled, as is standard practice for solver stability, so the model will not physically resist a self-intersecting command;) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.150 0.150 0.150 rg 204.0 336.9 Td (correctness is enforced by the offline reachability and pose tests instead.) Tj ET
