BT /F2 19.0 Tf 1.000 1.000 1.000 rg 46.0 576.0 Td (14.  Path to an Industry-Grade System) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.720 0.800 0.900 rg 46.0 558.5 Td (Ordered by payoff per unit of effort) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.5 Tf 0.100 0.280 0.480 rg 46.0 505.5 Td (Immediate - smoothness and robustness, small contained changes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 488.7 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 488.7 Td (Emit velocities with each trajectory point so the controllers produce cubic rather than linear interpolation - the single largest visual improvement available.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 472.4 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 472.4 Td (Trapezoidal velocity profiles and blended arcs for the base, replacing the current turn-drive-turn motion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 456.0 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 456.0 Td (Drive the arms through the FollowJointTrajectory action and use its result callback, eliminating the polling and settle heuristics entirely.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 439.7 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 439.7 Td (Low-pass filter the perception bearing and range feeding the servo loops.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.5 Tf 0.100 0.280 0.480 rg 46.0 416.7 Td (Structural - what makes the architecture defensible) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 399.9 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 399.9 Td (MoveIt 2 for both arms: planning groups, real collision checking and time-parameterised trajectories, which makes an arm-through-base fault structurally) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 386.6 Td (impossible.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 370.2 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 370.2 Td (Nav2 with SLAM or AMCL for the base, replacing dead reckoning, the scan hub heuristic and the bespoke docking routine.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 353.9 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 353.9 Td (A behaviour tree in place of the hand-rolled state machine, making recovery paths explicit and introspectable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 337.6 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 337.6 Td (Depth camera and point-cloud clustering with principal-axis estimation, which removes the object-orientation assumption altogether.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.5 Tf 0.100 0.280 0.480 rg 46.0 314.5 Td (Sim-to-real prerequisites) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 297.7 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 297.7 Td (Force-closure grasping with effort-based verification before lift, replacing the rigid constraint.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 281.4 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 281.4 Td (Safety layer: software emergency stop, command watchdog, controller-enforced workspace limits, guard active in every motion state.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.350 0.450 0.600 rg 60.0 265.1 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 70.0 265.1 Td (Continuous integration running the test suite and a headless mission test, plus a container image for reproducible runs.) Tj ET
